lomatic delegations to the winter  olympic games in beijing and olaf  schultz has left open so far whether he  would join this diplomatic you know what  is really a diplomatic boycott over  china's human rights record so we will  see you know will be interesting to  watch him take these very first steps as  german chancellor and we know that  domestically the most pressing problem  most pressing issue of course is the  pandemic and its impact what does  chancellor schultz  what does he inherit from angela merkel  yeah he inherits  a pretty bad situation you know germany  has been hit by the fourth wave of this  pandemic really hard with a couple of  hundred people dying every day um and  hospitals in some parts of the country  being overwhelmed by the amount of  patients um that that are coming in and  they have to send patients to other  parts other areas of the country because  their icus have reached capacity and so  olaf schultz and this new government  really have to hit the ground running  first you know on the top of the agenda  is to convince more people in germany to  get vaccinated as germany has quite a  low rate with uh 69.2 percent of adults  here having gotten two jobs so he really  needs to hit the ground running and and  prove that he can tackle the pandemic  that is very true leonie for hammerstein  reporting on what is an historic day  here at germany leone thank you  you
 

